    "answer": {
      "short": "Left horizontal length: $16\\text{ cm}$; right horizontal length: $5\\text{ cm}$.",
      "worked": "Let $h$ be the perpendicular height, $L$ and $R$ the left and right leg lengths, and $x$ and $y$ the left and right horizontal lengths, all in centimetres.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\nA &= \\frac{h(a+b)}{2}\\\\\n294 &= \\frac{h(14+35)}{2}\\\\\nh &= \\frac{2\\times294}{49}=12\\\\\nL &= \\frac{5h}{3}=\\frac{5\\times12}{3}=20\\\\\nR &= h+1=12+1=13\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nUsing Pythagoras’ theorem in each right triangle:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\nx &= \\sqrt{20^2-12^2}\\\\\nx &= 16\\text{ cm}\\\\\ny &= \\sqrt{13^2-12^2}\\\\\ny &= 5\\text{ cm}\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
